WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.225
Level one: the Big Picture.

2
00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:06.300
Start chaotic — everyone floods the wall with Domain Events.

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:11.575
Past tense, in the language of the business: “Ticket Purchased,” not “Purchase Ticket.”

4
00:00:11.575 --> 00:00:13.550
No discussion yet, just write.

5
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.300
Now enforce the timeline.

6
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:20.150
Slide the events left to right until they tell one shared story.

7
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:24.737
Mark the hotspots — the questions, conflicts and unknowns.

8
00:00:24.737 --> 00:00:27.462
Capture them in hot pink; don't resolve them.

9
00:00:27.462 --> 00:00:28.537
Add the people.

10
00:00:28.537 --> 00:00:30.362
Who triggers each event?

11
00:00:30.362 --> 00:00:32.062
The actors behind the story.

12
00:00:32.062 --> 00:00:38.412
Pivotal events sit on the boundary lines — where one context hands off to the next.

13
00:00:38.412 --> 00:00:44.662
Then walk the wall as one story — a single business narrative tying every event together.

14
00:00:44.662 --> 00:00:51.212
Arrow-vote the biggest problem: everyone points at what hurts most — consensus, without a meeting.

15
00:00:51.212 --> 00:00:52.462
And follow the money.

16
00:00:52.462 --> 00:00:57.212
Every step creates or destroys value — money, trust, time.

17
00:00:57.212 --> 00:01:01.912
Maximum knowledge, minimum notation — that's the Big Picture.

